# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole reactor).
#
# The Dockerfile copies the whole tree rather than a module list: `service` builds its dependency on
# `core` (internal, never published) from source, and a module list would need an edit every time a
# module is added. This file keeps that cheap — it drops everything the build does not need.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven build output. It is regenerated inside the build stage, it is the bulk of a working tree
# here, and a stale copy could shadow what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, so editing a README does not
# bust the copy layer.
*.md
docker

# What the release step exports next to the tree (the two SBOMs). Exported only after both images
# are pushed, and kept out of the context anyway, so they can never bust a copy layer.
.sbom
.sbom-companion
sbom-companion.json
